00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:38.820
Well then you can look at the national consortium
for the study of terrorism and responses to

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.820
terrorism.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:45.440
They maintain profiles of individual radicalization
in the United States.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:52.270
They look at individuals radicalized since
1948 and they have found that 40% are far

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.270
right.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:04:01.300
24% were Islamist, 17% are far left, and 18%
are what are called single issue individuals

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.950
who could be anywhere on the political spectrum
or even sort of outside of it.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.660
So no matter how you want to catalog this,
no matter what set of data you look at when

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:14.430
you look at radicalization in the United States,
when you look at what movements are leading

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.181
people to commit violence in order to try
